WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.188
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:16.285
Unit four: A2 Key: Listening. Today you will listen for names, numbers, times and short answers.

4
00:00:16.585 --> 00:00:19.249
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.363
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:25.020
Listen.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:27.981
Listen means to hear with attention.

8
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:29.910
Listen carefully.

9
00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:32.600
Your turn. Say: Listen.

10
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.212
Listen.

11
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:37.847
Spelling.

12
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.815
Spelling means the letters in a word.

13
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:42.650
Check the spelling.

14
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.879
Your turn. Say: Spelling.

15
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:49.746
Spelling.

16
00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.310
Number.

17
00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:55.233
Number means a figure like 7 or 15.

18
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:56.909
Write the number.

19
00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:59.844
Your turn. Say: Number.

20
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.666
Number.

21
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:05.174
Time.

22
00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:07.939
Time means hours and minutes.

23
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.702
What time is the lesson?

24
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:12.621
Your turn. Say: Time.

25
00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:16.189
Time.

26
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:17.847
Price.

27
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.861
Price means the cost of something.

28
00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.252
The price is five pounds.

29
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.270
Your turn. Say: Price.

30
00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:30.076
Price.

31
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:31.528
Day.

32
00:01:32.517 --> 00:01:34.853
Day means Monday, Tuesday and so on.

33
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.834
The party is on Friday.

34
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.487
Your turn. Say: Day.

35
00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:43.195
Day.

36
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.079
Second time.

37
00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:48.826
Second time means the audio plays twice.

38
00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:51.010
You hear it a second time.

39
00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:54.524
Your turn. Say: Second time.

40
00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.635
Second time.

41
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:00.164
Guess.

42
00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.312
Guess means to choose when unsure.

43
00:02:03.917 --> 00:02:05.429
Guess if you are unsure.

44
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:08.437
Your turn. Say: Guess.

45
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.220
Guess.

46
00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:16.522
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:20.997
Visal, how is the A2 Key Listening test organised?

48
00:02:22.083 --> 00:02:35.219
There are five parts. You listen to short conversations and messages and choose pictures, match information or write short answers such as names, numbers and times.

49
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:37.631
How can I prepare?

50
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:50.251
Read the questions before the audio and think about what type of answer you need. Practise names, numbers, dates and prices, because they are often tested.

51
00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.036
What if I miss an answer?

52
00:02:54.150 --> 00:03:02.062
You hear everything twice, so listen again for the missing detail. Never leave a blank, and check your spelling when you write.

53
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.677
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:09.200
Grammar focus: Strategy: predict, listen, write.

55
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.640
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.768
The lesson starts at half past four.

57
00:03:14.683 --> 00:03:17.043
The ticket costs fifteen pounds.

58
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.553
Read before you listen, predict the kind of answer, and use the second listening to check. Always write something.

59
00:03:25.317 --> 00:03:28.828
Be careful! Don't say: I leave an answer blank.

60
00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:33.231
Say: I always write an answer.

61
00:03:33.531 --> 00:03:34.926
Never leave blanks.

62
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:38.165
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:38.967 --> 00:03:40.548
Listening for Details.

64
00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:42.917
A girl calls a swimming club.

65
00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:46.270
She asks what time the lesson starts.

66
00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:50.450
The man says it starts at half past four on Thursday.

67
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.931
He says a ticket costs fifteen pounds.

68
00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:57.362
She writes the time and the price on her form.

69
00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:02.643
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:03.483 --> 00:04:05.309
You hear each recording blank.

71
00:04:05.609 --> 00:04:09.204
A, three times. B, twice. C, once.

72
00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.557
The answer is B: twice.

73
00:04:15.717 --> 00:04:17.635
What time does the lesson start?

74
00:04:17.935 --> 00:04:22.865
A, half past six. B, five o'clock. C, half past four.

75
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.177
The answer is C: half past four.

76
00:04:30.317 --> 00:04:32.514
The ticket costs blank pounds.

77
00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:36.165
A, fifteen. B, fifty. C, five.

78
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.816
The answer is A: fifteen.

79
00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.741
Before listening you should blank.

80
00:04:45.041 --> 00:04:49.704
A, write nothing. B, read the questions. C, close your eyes.

81
00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.603
The answer is B: read the questions.

82
00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.378
What should you do if unsure?

83
00:04:58.678 --> 00:05:02.146
A, leave blank. B, stop. C, write something.

84
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.408
The answer is C: write something.

85
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.694
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.770
How do you prepare for the Listening paper?

87
00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:26.223
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.523 --> 00:05:39.917
I read the questions first and decide what kind of answer I need, for example a time or a price. When I listen, I write the answer. The second time I listen again to check my answer and my spelling.

89
00:05:40.217 --> 00:05:41.903
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:42.817 --> 00:05:48.743
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: predict, listen, write.

91
00:05:49.043 --> 00:05:53.390
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:56.273
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

93
00:05:56.573 --> 00:05:59.841
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

